{
  "comment": "#615 L2: how each material takes a studio light, checked with scripts/lighting/check_materials.py l2 (its docstring names what each check reads). 1rx1 at 1280x720 on black, depth_cue 0, subjects grey80 alone (a surface holds nothing, so glass shows only itself). Rig W, white (warmth 6500): key orbit -40 pitch 30 beam 55 softness 0.5 intensity 1, fill orbit 55 pitch 5 beam 80 softness 0.8 intensity 0.5, rim orbit 150 pitch 25 beam 50 softness 0.4 intensity 0.8, radius 3, ambient 0.06, and an explicit centre and size (the extent of m). Its variants: hi1/hi0 every highlight 1/0; dark every intensity 0 at classic 0, dark_c1 the same at classic 1; dim1/dim0 every intensity 0.3 at highlight 0.5/0 (peaks under the 8-bit knee); dimdark every intensity 0. Tags: <mat>_<rep>[_sh]_<variant>_rt<n> (rep surface, sticks, spheres or dots = surface dots as sphere impostors: surface_type 1, dot_as_spheres 1; frosted = frosted_glass; _sh: the key shadowed and metal_shadows 1). tint_metallic_{t0,tab}_*: the same metallic on one saturated base (0.85, 0.45, 0.10) with material_env 2 (no environment), t0 at Custom <rep>_material_tint 0 and tab at the table's; tint_{default,plastic}_* are the neutral controls. <mat>_surface_{dim0,dimdark}: material_env 2. rubber_k3z/rubber_k4z/jelly_k3z: Custom surface_material_knob3/knob4 0 (rubber's Highlight and Sheen, jelly's Wet highlight). lobe_*: one white key at highlight 1, material_env 1 (the studio lobe beside the environment lobe; for the eye). The frozen harness (render.py) installs its own rig for \"rig\": \"on\" by calling cmd.set_lights after each scene's lines; the extra lines wrap cmd.set_lights once per process (hasattr guard: the app runs the script twice) and install cmd._l615_rig instead. Every scene sets cmd._l615_rig as its last line. Checked in CI by testing/tests/raymol/lighting_material_check.py.",
  "base": null,
  "rig": "on",
  "size": [1280, 720],
  "extra": [
    "import math as _l615_math",
    "_l615_mn, _l615_mx = cmd.get_extent('m')",
    "_l615_c = [(a + b) / 2.0 for a, b in zip(_l615_mn, _l615_mx)]",
    "_l615_s = _l615_math.sqrt(sum((b - a) ** 2 for a, b in zip(_l615_mn, _l615_mx))) / 2.0",
    "if not hasattr(cmd, '_l615_set'): cmd._l615_set = cmd.set_lights",
    "cmd.set_lights = lambda rig, _c=cmd: _c._l615_set(rig if getattr(_c, '_l615_rig', None) is None else (_c._l615_rig(rig) if callable(_c._l615_rig) else _c._l615_rig))",
    "_l615_key = {'name': 'key', 'orbit': -40.0, 'pitch': 30.0, 'radius': 3.0, 'beam': 55.0, 'softness': 0.5, 'color': [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], 'warmth': 6500.0, 'intensity': 1.0, 'highlight': 0.5}",
    "_l615_fill = {'name': 'fill', 'orbit': 55.0, 'pitch': 5.0, 'radius': 3.0, 'beam': 80.0, 'softness': 0.8, 'color': [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], 'warmth': 6500.0, 'intensity': 0.5, 'highlight': 0.5}",
    "_l615_rim = {'name': 'rim', 'orbit': 150.0, 'pitch': 25.0, 'radius': 3.0, 'beam': 50.0, 'softness': 0.4, 'color': [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], 'warmth': 6500.0, 'intensity': 0.8, 'highlight': 0.5}",
    "_l615_var = {'hi1': (None, 1.0, 0.0), 'hi0': (None, 0.0, 0.0), 'dark': (0.0, 0.5, 0.0), 'dark_c1': (0.0, 0.5, 1.0), 'dim1': (0.3, 0.5, 0.0), 'dim0': (0.3, 0.0, 0.0), 'dimdark': (0.0, 0.0, 0.0)}",
    "_l615_light = lambda light, v, shadow: dict(light, intensity=light['intensity'] if _l615_var[v][0] is None else _l615_var[v][0], highlight=_l615_var[v][1], shadow=bool(shadow and light['name'] == 'key'))",
    "_l615_W = lambda v, shadow=False: {'version': 1, 'enabled': True, 'ambient': 0.06, 'classic': _l615_var[v][2], 'centre': list(_l615_c), 'size': _l615_s, 'lights': [_l615_light(l, v, shadow) for l in (_l615_key, _l615_fill, _l615_rim)]}",
    "_l615_lobe = lambda: {'version': 1, 'enabled': True, 'ambient': 0.06, 'classic': 0.0, 'centre': list(_l615_c), 'size': _l615_s, 'lights': [dict(_l615_key, highlight=1.0)]}",
    "cmd.set('depth_cue', 0)",
    "cmd.set_color('l615_orange', [0.85, 0.45, 0.10])"
  ],
  "scenes": [
    {"tag": "default_surface_hi1_rt0", "from": "surface_rt0", "lines": ["cmd.color('grey80', 'm')", "cmd._l615_rig = _l615_W('hi1')"]},
